 supplement same idea we  do PI minus 3 PI over 4 you want to get  common denominator so I'm gonna multiply  by 4 over 4 so that comes out to 1 PI  over 4 this is positive so there is a  supplement PI over 4 so this has been a  little bit about how to find complements  and supplements working with the Radian  angle measurements and you can see  sometimes you don't get a complement or  you might not get a supplement if it  turns out to be negative but again the  key is just to use PI over 2 minus the  angle or PI minus the angle and you've  got it I'll see you in the next video
 

